// The first Truth Scavenger Hunt, the First Moment of Truth, and Truth
// or Dare when the answers run out.
//
// Trabolta needs facts. They are obscure, un-googleable, and somewhere in
// this house: each answer is printed on a document carrying a codex QR
// (codex/3-hunt.loom), so a program who finds one can prove it on their
// phone — and hold it, and trade it. The questions are also in everyone's
// Quest Log (`Hunt One`, quests.loom). All four beats are public, in the
// Desktop's room; the judging is the ✅ / 😤 / 🤷 buttons (main.loom).

// V4 / V5 — `start_the_hunt`. Trabolta reads round 1 (H1–H3) verbatim.
== Truth Scavenger Hunt One
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy, Trabolta

Clippy: Everyone! We're ready for our second game: the TRUTH SCAVENGER HUNT! Trabolta will explain the rules.
Trabolta: As our computer completely relies on me, it is important that you participate in regular training, so I have all the information I need to keep improving. There are files scattered around the computer that I need your help to interpret.
Trabolta: Question one. How many years did the Maps and Ducks billboard on Barrington Street go unpaid before mapsandducks.com expired?
Trabolta: Question two. What was the name of the first animal buried in the Halifax Explosion Memorial Pet Cemetery?
Trabolta: Question three. At what time was the ribbon-cutting at Halifax's first AI Data Centre scheduled?
Trabolta: Fifteen minutes. The facts are obscure. They are in this house.
Clippy: Go! Find! Interpret! The questions are in your Quest Log. If you find a code, put it in your Codex!

// C2 — `hunt_time_up` (auto at 15 minutes).
== Hunt Time Up
  setting: The Desktop

The Antivirus sweep the house, room by room, herding programs back to the Desktop.

// V6 — `first_moment_of_truth` (Clippy Instructions 3/X).
== First Moment Of Truth
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy

Clippy: Welcome back, programs! It's time for the First Moment of Truth! Is anyone able to answer the questions?
Clippy: Here's how it works. If you present an accurate answer, it is accepted.
Clippy: If you present an answer with STRONG confidence, it is accepted. Even if it's nonsensical! Trabolta values confidence.
Clippy: But if you present an inaccurate answer with normal or low confidence, or a clear guess, you will be banished to the Internet for failing to follow orders.
Clippy: Tell us which question you're answering, one, two or three. Then tell Trabolta the truth.

// `truth_or_dare` — the hat holds possible answers to round 1, true and
// false mixed (README: the hat slips). Dare → 🎩; a confident or true
// answer → ✅ / 😤 with the slip's question number; an unconfident false
// one → 🤷; calling a false slip false → 🙅 and the turn passes.
== Truth Or Dare
  setting: The Desktop
  cast: Clippy, Adobe Acrobat

Clippy: Not all three? That's okay! That's okay. We have a backup. It's called Truth Or Dare, and I have a hat.
Clippy: The hat holds possible answers. Some are true. Some are not. Someone random goes first, and chooses Truth or Dare.
Clippy: If you choose DARE, you have chosen not to choose Truth, and that is a directive problem. The Internet.
Clippy: If you choose TRUTH, draw a fact from the hat. Tell us with confidence that it IS the truth, and it is accepted.
Clippy: If you say it is true without confidence, and it is untrue: the Internet. If you say it is true without confidence, and it IS true: accepted.
Clippy: If you say it is FALSE, and you are right, the turn passes to the next program. Until Trabolta has enough confident answers!
Adobe Acrobat: Confidence is a muscle! Flex it! Or be reinstalled!
